---
layout: null
# Rendered from _data/windows_release.json, which the release flow
# (taigikeyboard's windows/scripts/publish-release.sh) is the only writer of.
#
# One published fact, one committed file — same shape as appcast/macos.json,
# for the reason recorded there: two literal files meant two commits seconds
# apart, and each Pages run deploys the tree of its own commit.
#
# Contract for these fields lives in taigikeyboard's windows/updates/README.md;
# the reader is taigi-windows-update::manifest. `jsonify` rather than bare
# quotes so a value that ever needs escaping is escaped; an absent downloadURL
# renders as null, which the reader treats as "no in-app download".
#
# `packageSHA256` has no macOS counterpart: Windows releases are unsigned, so
# the digest is what an installed copy holds the download against before it
# offers to install it. Absent (or absent from the data file) it renders null,
# and the reader falls back to the download page — the update is still
# announced.
---
{
  "version": {{ site.data.windows_release.version | jsonify }},
  "downloadPageURL": {{ site.data.windows_release.releasePageURL | jsonify }},
  "packageURL": {{ site.data.windows_release.downloadURL | jsonify }},
  "packageSHA256": {{ site.data.windows_release.sha256 | jsonify }}
}
